SOAPBOX: This was another WQ6X QRP WPX RTTY GiG, but from Anza this time.
SOAPBOX: This year's Weird Prefix (WPX) RTTY contest was a mixed-BAG.
SOAPBOX: Running QRP is always a challenge altho having access to the stacked yagi's
SOAPBOX: and 80-meter 4-Square made a difference in signal strength.
SOAPBOX: My biggest beef is stations who start calling CQ EXACTLY ZERO-BEAT with my
SOAPBOX: oddball chosen run frequencies (Ex: 21111.11, 21131.31, 14088.88, 7091.91, etc.).
SOAPBOX: There is no way dozens of stations end up EXACTLY on my run frequency by accident.
SOAPBOX: While there was a nice opening to EU on 40-meters, overall, EU access was down,
SOAPBOX: altho working SM2M (via LP) on 15-meters when pointed at Aussie land was certainly
SOAPBOX: a kick. As the weekend progressed, solar-induced geomagnetic noise became quite
SOAPBOX: a problem. Because I was using the Stereo-RTTY method, turning on the Elecraft
SOAPBOX: DNR actually rendered signals less copy-able, so I dealt with the noise.
SOAPBOX: Read all about this and other GiGs at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
